==English==

===Etymology===
From the Middle English ''[[ransoun]],'' from the Old French ''[[rançon]],'' from the {{L.}} ''[[redemption]]-, [[redemptio-]]'' (see [[redemption]]). Entered English ca. the 13th century

===Noun===
'''ransom'''

# [[Money]] paid for the [[free]]ing of a [[hostage]].

